        <mxCell id="wOe7zqhs2_QcdCpgvtuy-42" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Tasks&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Create workspace: click on workspace in Fabrick --&amp;gt; click on new workspace, then give a unique name --choose trial or Fabric&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Create lakehouse: click on New Item ---&amp;gt; select lakehouse --&amp;gt; Give a unique name --&amp;gt; initially you see only tables and files, just similar to a Databricks&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Create Folder: click on 3 dots next to Files, select new subfolder, give a name --&amp;gt; then upload a file by clicking on ellipsis, then click on upload file, then browse file, then upload.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Creating Table from file: click ellipsis next to sales file, then create -- load to a table -- new table&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Create Shortcut: Click on the folder, then choose shortcut, then select one of the storage like&amp;nbsp; One Lake(Like Deltalake), S3, ADLS Gen2, GCS.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Create a querying platform like SQL Server Management Studio: click on Lakehouse on the left side button, then SQL Analytics endpoint, then this gives you another view like SSMS&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;This view has a hierarchy like&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Schema&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;DB&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Tables&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Queries -&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;my queries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;- Shared queries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Model Layouts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;You can query a table now in this view&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;You can use AI to ask an explanatory query it will give annotations&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;You can visually work out the using query canvas&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Drag and drop a table, then it will give a visual representation, then you can click on the + button at the end and create new sub-tables with transformations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Model layout: You can create model layouts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Reporting: This will give you Power BI integration to create new reports&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Reports --&amp;gt; Create new report --&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp; will give the report in the Power BI UI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Raw data to Report jurney every thing in one place that is in Lakehouse.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="400" x="80" y="10170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
